Oops, I did it again!

lawful - Valkyrie - female (no male valks allowed) - Gabkin (all of my
chars have this name)

I think the deciding factor was the early +1 boots of speed (lvl 2 I
think).Apart from that the early game was unspectacular (no early
wishes or /oPoly this time).
Got excalibur fairly early (from minetown ISTR) and used that most of
the game along with the watch captains silver saber (gotta start
practising those skills early!).
Sokoban gave me "oR which I suppose helped out some, but I would have
preferred the bag...
I used a plain sack for ages!
Around lvl 15 I found one of my bones containing SDSM and
greyswandir.I immediately went to my sokoban stash, enchanted up
grayswandir to +7 and used that along with a +1 longsword for a long
time. (Dual wielding rocks!)
I did the quest and camped about on home level with my two rings of
hunger, scoffing giants like candy...
Fort Ludios never did show up (damn).

Unfortunately my SDSM and (fireproofed) +4 elven cloak got vaporized
by some stupid golden naga in the maze between medusa and the castle.
I used some levitating boots to get around the castle and beat the
dragons senseless (and got green scales, yay! out of a
silver,grey,green and red dragon combo).
I think I cleared out the castle by standing just behind the doorway,
burning Elbereth on the floor (my AC was something sad like -10, half
of which was from protection) and slowly offing the soldiers one at a
time.I know now I should have used the drawbridge trick but I didn't
(OTOH I would have lost all of their items that way).
I used the wand to complete my ascension kit (SDSM,[oPower,[oMR,magic
marker,2 scrolls of charging and 2 scrolls of genocide).
Then I went back to my stash, enchanted, alchemized, ID'ed etc etc.

I then decided that as I have everything that I need (AC:-34 or so, +7
grayswandir,+7 longsword,speed,MR,reflection,TC) I would make the
final rites as fast as possible (Fate starts laughing).
So I jumped to the VoTD, ran though (didn't even kill everything like
I usually do), descended to Gehennom, invoked the orb and jumped to
the bottom level.
I found the Vibrating square and marked it by snapping a wand of
digging (usually I dig out a HUGE cavern around it and make an ASCII
arrow with gold pieces,wand of fire and liberal use of 'Elbereth').

Then I decided to get a greater demon to help me map the levels.
(arch-liches were already geno'ed).
So I loafed around while some demons swiped ineffectually at me and
summoned more demons.
...
Many demons later some greater demon arrived (I cant remember who).
I dispatched all of his minions, wielded my +0 longsword and swiped at
the named demon a few times.He 'ported to the stairs and I found him
with my blindfold and telepathy.I dug a route to him, chased him
upstairs and repeated. At some point I accidentally hit him with the
+7 grayswandir and +7 longsword and killed him (oops). It was an
accident I swear!
I then used Orcus to finish mapping out gehennom and had it all mapped
out in great time (for a combat-wombat anyway).I think it was about
turn 30000.

Then I checked my spoilers and saw that Vlads towers would be between
level 38 and 43.
I searched those levels and found neither hide nor hair of an
additional upstairs!
instead of checking the validity of my data (out of date spoilers) I
decided that I must have missed it in this @*&^#$@^$^! maze.
So I started digging...
Some Umber hulks arrived and helped me dig...
About 30000 turns later I stepped back, surveyed my impressive
archaelogical excavation... and screamed with horror!
NO sign of any upstairs!!
Dylan O' Donnel helpfully pointed out that my spoilers were out of
date and that the tower would actually be between 34 and 39 (thanks
Dylan). I found it on level 34, naturally.

After that, things were pretty uneventful. I went over to Rodney's
place and did some interior decorating with the aid of a cockatrice.
The cockatrice corpse ran out just as I had rodney in sight so I had
to beat him to death the old-fashioned way...

Molochs sanctum was a breeze, I think the most worrying moment was
when the rodney twin stole my orb of fate...
I grabbed the amulet and ran upstairs.
The mysterious force threw me back at least ten times, very annoying!

Went to my stash and did some last-minute sorting, grabbing
essentials, adjusting autopickup options etc.

The planes were pretty unexceptional except in the fact that they were
a breeze! 
EARTH:
(a)pply orb of fate, search for portal.Zap wands of digging. Done.
I found a magic marker en route.
AIR:
Put on boots of levitaion.
Beat all of the air elementals to death with 'nary a scratch while I
Searched for the portal using the amulet of yendor and its hot/cold
status.
FIRE:
(a)pply orb of fate, search for portal.Float over to it without
attacking anyone on this plane.
WATER:
put on amulet of yendor and wandered about aimlessly, beating poor
little fishes to death occasionally.
Eventually wandered into the portal!

and finally 
ASTRAL:
Went left to famine first, he fell to one attack, beat everyone
senseless (except the priest) and found a neutral altar.D'oh!
Went to the middle next and bumped into pestilence.He was a bit of a
pest but nothing +7 Grayswandir and an unihorn couldn't handle.Found
my altar here but decided to see if I could grab a t-shirt off someone
around here. (last minute greed)
So I left the temple and beat up the various characters loafing
about.None of them had any t-shirts (one of them had +6 frostbane
though).Oh well, couldn't be helped!

I went back to my altar and offered the amulet.
Details follow...

It was interesting how easy astral was for a dual-wielding valk.
My last ascension with a slashem vampiric wizard had to fight for his
life here. 
+2 magicbane hardly does any damage and all of the Angels have
reflection, negating most offensive spells, whereas dual weapons rips
everything to little shreds in 1-3 hits.

